$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Procedure for the Synthesis of the
Carboxamides 1a−i, 1bA−bC, 1dA, 1eA, and 1fA. The corresponding
carboxylic acid (1.5 mmol) was dissolved in SOCl2 (4 mmol) and stirred
for 24 h at rt under a nitrogen atmosphere. After this period, the
reaction mixture was concentrated in vacuum and diluted with anhydrous
DCM (3 mL) under a nitrogen atmosphere. Then the corresponding acid
chloride in DCM was added to a separate RB flask containing amine (1
mmol) and Et3N (1.1 mmol) in anhydrous DCM (2 mL) under a nitrogen
atmosphere. The reaction mixture was stirred at rt for 10 min, and then
the reaction mixture was refluxed for 12 h under a nitrogen atmosphere.
After this period, the reaction mixture was diluted with DCM (5 mL) and
washed with water followed by saturated aqueous NaHCO3 solution. The
combined organic layers were dried over anhydrous Na2SO4 and concentrated
in vacuum, and purification of the resulting reaction mixture by column
chromatography (EtOAc/ hexanes = 30:70). The corresponding cyclic ether
carboxamides 1a−i, 1bA−bC, 1dA, 1eA, and 1fA.
N-(Quinolin-8-yl)tetrahydrofuran-2-carboxamide (1a). Following the
general procedure, 1a was obtained after purification by column
chromatography on silica gel (EtOAc:hexanes = 30:70). HPLC analysis
performed using OD-H (0.46 cm IDR 25 cm length) as a chiral column.
Eluents, flow rate, detection are listed here. Chiral HPLC: OD-H
(isocratic, hexane/isopropanol 90:10:, 1.0 mL/min, PDA at 323.5 nm)
N-((Tetrahydrofuran-2-yl)methyl)picolinamide (1dA). Following the general
procedure, 1dA was obtained after purification by column chromatography
on silica gel (EtOAc:hexanes = 40:60). Dark brown color liquid; yield:
80% (165 mg). IR (DCM): 3480, 1668, 1590, 1077, 751 cm-1; 1H NMR (400
MHz, CDCl3): δ 8.57−8.55 (m, 1H), 8.36 (br s, 1H), 8.19 (d, 1H, J = 7.8
Hz), 7.84 (dt, 1H, J 1 = 7.7 Hz, J 2 = 1.7 Hz), 7.44−7.40 (m, 1H),
4.13−4.07 (m, 1H), 3.95−3.90 (m, 1H), 3.82−3.71 (m, 2H), 3.47−3.41 (m,
1H), 2.07−1.99 (m, 1H), 1.95−1.87 (m, 2H), 1.68−1.59 (m, 1H); 13C NMR
(100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 164.4, 149.8, 148.1, 137.3, 126.1, 122.2, 77.8, 68.3,
43.2, 28.8, 25.9; HRMS (ESI): m/z [M + H]+ calcd for C11H15N2O2:
207.1134; found 207.1157.
